      \field{abstract}{For large state-space Markovian Decision Problems MonteCarlo planning is one of the few viable approaches to ﬁnd near-optimal solutions. In this paper we introduce a new algorithm, UCT, that applies bandit ideas to guide Monte-Carlo planning. In ﬁnite-horizon or discounted MDPs the algorithm is shown to be consistent and ﬁnite sample bounds are derived on the estimation error due to sampling. Experimental results show that in several domains, UCT is signiﬁcantly more eﬃcient than its alternatives.}
